{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502761-what-s-the-craziest-film-you-ever-watched","id":1502761,"title":"What's the craziest film you ever watched?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-11T09:58:36-08:00","id":1502761,"title":"What's the craziest film you ever watched?","content":"I just watched Willy In Wonderland with Nic Cage and it's as crazy film where he doesn't speak a single line or know anything of his backstory or even his name and fights possessed robots to pay off his flat tires for his car.<br /> <br /> What movies have you watched and wondered how crazy it was that it was green lit outside of Steven Seagal films?<br /> <br /> I should point out some of these crazy movies are a guilty pleasure like Willy Wonderland or some of Jean Claude Van Dame, Mel Gibson or Dolph Lundgren for that matter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-18-2023, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T12:20:04-08:00","id":1502766,"title":"","content":"Irreversible and not in a good way.. Very hard watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T18:09:39-08:00","id":1502799,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highlander_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander</a>. A movie where the one thing that actually ended up happening in real life was the thing that broke my suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> I don't think people realize just how batshit bonkers that film must have been when it came out. I certainly didn't realize it until after watching it several times, partly because I had already seen a few episodes of the tv show so I was already kind of on board with the concept. I actually ran a scenario in my head where I somehow traveled back to the late 70s/ early 80s and had to explain the movie to people, and the more I tried to explain it, the more confusing it sounded. But it's near the climax of the film where what sadly turned out to be the most plausible scenario seemed to take the film off the rails (at least for me).<br /> <br /> By the time the third act starts, anyone watching it has been asked to just accept a lot. You're asked to just accept there are magical people who can smuggle their swords almost anywhere, and could theoretically live forever (I say theoretically, because the plot of this movie is about how these &quot;immortal&quot; people fight until the loser finds out just how <i>mortal</i> they are). You're asked to accept a French actor as a Medieval Scotsman and a Scottish actor as an ancient Egyptian. So when a guy in a t-shirt with a picture of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Basil&#39;s_Cathedral\" target=\"_blank\">St. Basil's Cathedral</a> overlayed with iron sights, and a caption saying &quot;Hey Moscow, Up yours!&quot; printed on it, loads the trunk of a red sport's car with <i>machine guns</i>, slams the lid shut, and starts driving said car (with an <i>Uzi</i> on the passenger seat) around NYC looking for someone to shoot, the movie became too much for me.<br /> <br /> See, I first saw this film maybe eight to ten years after it came out. This was early to mid 90s, <i>just before</i> the world wide web was taking off, it was basically the last time someone outside the US (like me) could live blissfully ignorant of the Second Amendment, like I did. Considering that the first swordfight in the movie ended with the protagonist stashing his sword before being arrested by an army of cops, and then chased by a police helicopter after retrieving his sword, I just could see how this nutter introduced out of nowhere could just go almost anywhere in the city looking to shoot someone... And then a few years later, Columbine High School happened, and Red Lake High School happened a few years after <i>that</i>, and then a year later West Nickel Mines, Amish School, and Virginia Tech a year after that... And <a href=\"https://www.usnews.com/news/us/articles/2022-05-24/a-look-at-some-of-the-deadliest-us-school-shootings\" target=\"_blank\">now this stuff</a> barely makes the news. <br /> <br /> And the craziest part, after Moscow shirt guy (he's named Kirk Matunas, according to Wikipedia, but he'll always be Moscow shirt guy to me) has been questioned by the detectives investigating the &quot;rash of beheadings occurring in NYC,&quot; the Lieutenant describes him as &quot;a good kid.&quot; This was a nut with a car full of guns looking for an excuse to shoot someone, and the Lieutenant calls him a good kid. Even the script writers didn't seem to realize how screwed up this character was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T04:51:47-08:00","id":1502826,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/enH3xA4mYcY\" target=\"_blank\">Sorry To Bother You</a>. Saw it in the middle of a trip, and had no idea what it was about beforehand. One of the few movies I've walked out of feeling both confused and deeply uncomfortable about, although it might have been better if I'd gone in knowing what to expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:21:58-08:00","id":1502851,"title":"","content":"Highlander is one of those films is where you just go with it and just go with the crazy premise. Though the first film and tv series were the only good ones to follow, but I did like Colin MCcloud in Highlander anime movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","